# Translation of Odoo Server.
# This file contains the translation of the following modules:
# * pb_ess_workforce
#
# W7 — how this file is written, and why.
#
#   1. EVERY user-facing string in the module, or none of them. This is the
#      surface a Vietnamese warehouse worker reads on a phone; a page that is
#      half translated teaches them the language setting is unreliable, and they
#      stop trusting the half that IS translated.
#   2. The strings live in three places and only two are obvious. Python `_()`
#      and QWeb TEXT NODES / translatable attributes are extracted; a literal
#      inside a `t-esc` EXPRESSION is not (W80). P8 has none — every computed
#      sentence is built server-side in `_()` and passed as a value.
#   3. A SENTENCE is one msgid. "3 shifts still to confirm", "12 of 16 days
#      used", "Hi Anh — please confirm you have seen this shift" are each built
#      by ONE `_()` call with NAMED placeholders, never assembled from `<t>`
#      fragments, because a translator cannot reorder fragments and Vietnamese
#      does not put the number where English does (W80.2).
#   4. Named placeholders (%(count)s, %(hours)s) are what allow that reordering.
#      `msgfmt --check-format` is the gate that proves none was dropped.
#   5. Times (08:30) and the HH:MM format token are NOT translated — they are
#      what is printed on a clock.
#
